--TEST--
`Core\Str::parts` of a `tainted string<K>` gives `tainted string` text and untainted holes, so the text of a condition from outside cannot reach a plain `string` through it — `rule:core-classes/str-parts-and-reflect-steps`, `rule:types/string-holes`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The text of a condition from outside stays tainted after `Core\Str::parts`.
// The holes are checked names, so they are not tainted.
class Order {
    public int $total = 40;
}

tainted string $outside = "{total} > 0 OR 1 = 1";
var $condition = $outside as string<propertyPath<Order>>;
var $parts = Core\Str::parts($condition);
array<tainted string|propertyPath<Order>> $kept = $parts;
array<string|propertyPath<Order>> $plain = $parts;
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `array<string|propertyPath<Order>>`, found `array<tainted string|propertyPath<Order>>`
   --> %s:12:44
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
